---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Saved searches — mgz-pkmn docs"
  description="Saved searches in mgz-pkmn: name a lookup to keep it, then click to rerun with its input and results restored. Distinct from the client-side Recent history."
  current="/docs/saved-searches"
  icon="bookmark"
  accent="ember"
  eyebrow="Your stuff"
  heading="Saved searches"
  lede="Some lists you run once. Others you come back to every time a new set drops or a show comes around. Saving a search keeps the second kind one click away."
>
  <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Name it to keep it
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Run a <a href="/docs/search" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Search</a>,
    then give it a name to save it. Every completed lookup is persisted under the
    hood, but only the ones you name surface in the
    <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Searches</strong>
    tab of your <a href="/docs/backpack" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Backpack</a>
    — so the tab stays a short, curated shelf rather than a pile of everything
    you've ever typed.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Pick up where you left off
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Click a saved search to hydrate the editor and results with its input and the
    view you'd set — sort, filters, the lot — exactly as you left them. It's the
    same list, ready to reprice against today's market.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-palm-300 bg-palm-50 p-5 dark:border-sun-300/40 dark:bg-sun-300/5">
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-600 dark:text-sand-200">
      <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Saved vs. Recent:</strong>
      the <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Recent</strong>
      tab is a quick, browser-local history of inputs for one-tap re-runs; saved
      searches are named, durable, and tied to your account. Sign in to keep them
      across devices.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
